      "obligation": "refuter:9:1",
      "id": "def-the-level-one-vector-representation-its-affinization-and-energy-function",
      "location": "Statement (iii)",
      "defect": "overstrong-title-or-statement",
      "evidence": "Statement (iii) says “The same statements hold on the affinization” after (i) asserts that the finite crystal is perfect, including bijective ε and φ maps. But the Definition gives ε(u_m)=Λ_{j-1}^cl and φ(u_m)=Λ_j^cl, so distinct basis elements u_m and u_{m-e} have identical ε and φ. Those maps are not injective on B_aff; the proof in 2.1 establishes bar and string properties, not perfectness of the affinization.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "20aff2aec58a42f7e7707d42a1d259243b88383ca3e1243d0cef1dc832744c4b"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:9:2",
      "id": "lem-fixed-residue-node-cubes-realize-fock-i-strings-and-crystal-lattices",
      "location": "Statement",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The Statement assigns “+ when the slot is empty (addable) and - when it is empty (removable).” A removable cell is occupied, not empty; as written the two signs do not encode the two slot states. Proof 3.1 confirms the intended polarity by setting ε_s=1 on an empty slot and -1 on an occupied slot.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "observed_sha256": "06d7ad290691680e48853a3e915a37fea5ee06a895402ff1d5168d7481e6fab2"
    },
    {
      "obligation": "refuter:9:3",
      "id": "quantum-affine-type-a-and-level-one-fock-space",
      "location": "Semi-infinite wedges and the Fock space paragraph",
      "defect": "ill-formed",
      "evidence": "The page gives the index formula as “i_k=Λ_k-k+1+M.” Elsewhere on this page Λ denotes a fundamental weight, while the scoped Fock-space definition gives i_k=M+λ_k-k+1 with λ_k the kth part of the partition. The capital-weight expression is not an integer index formula and is ill-typed.",
      "severity": "nonfatal",
      "observed_sha256": "d551528b584516544a589ad6090f4cec3eb4c8921a0dbc4637aa93533a451acf"
    }
